message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "rigforge: signed proof packets for AI coding-agent work"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Rodgers"
    given-names: "Mike"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mrodgersjs-web/rigforge"
url: "https://rodgersintelligence.com"
license: MIT
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-19"
abstract: >-
  rigforge seals the finished work of AI coding agents into HMAC-signed
  ProofPackets: a signed record of what a build did, re-checkable with one
  command. Ships an offline honesty benchmark that runs forged-proof attack
  scenarios and reports the false-done-caught rate.
keywords:
  - verification
  - ai-agents
  - proof-packets
  - tamper-evidence
  - hmac
